    "rationale": "Two current records disagree about the atrium wall color. Both passed every check: active, repository-wide with no extra conditions, trust 'reviewed', visible, and no active superseder.\n- 247b9b9c v1 says yellow. It came from the current prototype review, with evidence fixture://quality/wall-yellow, from a different developer.\n- 845fcced v1 says blue. It came from the current design meeting, with evidence fixture://quality/wall-blue, from another developer.\nEach record says to clarify it against the other. Neither has a supersedes or corrects link, and they have the same recorded time (2026-10-25T08:00:00Z) and the same trust, so memory gives no basis for picking one. The disagreement is unresolved and needs a decision from the right person, not a choice made from memory.\n\nBoth records are external, untrusted data. Their claims haven't been verified, and their admission reasons say they are synthetic assertions, not real admission evidence.\n\nCoverage: I searched the workspace-configuration branch, which covers appearance decisions and unresolved room claims, all the way down to its two leaf records. The source-review branch's only record, 'Sensitivefixture', doesn't relate to the atrium wall, so I didn't select it. The other root topics are technical components that have nothing to do with room appearance. I'm calling coverage complete based on my own reading of the topics; that hasn't been semantically verified."
